WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.396
The method starts from the kernel-ridge estimator
and splits the test error into a bias term and a variance term,

00:00:07.476 --> 00:00:09.711
each bounded with high probability.

00:00:09.791 --> 00:00:13.416
The key ingredients: careful algebra on the ridge terms,

00:00:13.496 --> 00:00:18.907
a sub-Gaussian covariance concentration inequality,
and a Neumann-series expansion.

00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:21.950
That lets the bounds hold for any ridge value.
